# This file is used by the build system to adjust CSS and JS output to support the specified browsers below.
# For additional information regarding the format and rule options, please see:
# https://github.com/browserslist/browserslist#queries

# Ionic 9's supported browsers: https://ionicframework.com/docs/updating/9-0
#
# Stated as explicit floors rather than the CLI's default "last N versions". A relative query drifts upward with every
# browser release and silently narrows what the bundle runs on: it had already reached iOS 18 while the app still ships
# an iOS 16 deployment target, so the output would not have parsed on a device the app installs on happily. A floor only
# moves when someone decides to move it.
#
# One deliberate deviation: Ionic supports Firefox 75+, but 75 predates top-level await, which Angular's own test-bed
# bootstrap emits — so the unit tests will not compile against it. Firefox is never a shipping target here (this app runs
# in the iOS WKWebView and the Android System WebView; Firefox only ever sees `ng serve`), so the floor is the first
# version that supports the syntax Angular emits.

# You can see what browsers were selected by your queries by running:
#   npx browserslist

Chrome >= 89
ChromeAndroid >= 89
Edge >= 89
Firefox >= 89
Safari >= 16
iOS >= 16
